From 6039889519529dbed6357c97cdf5ef648de98886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:41:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] IOP ioman: file operations reach the registered device's
 functions

ioman handled only AddDrv (20) and DelDrv (21): a driver like MCMAN could register its "mc" device, but open,
read, close and the rest were unhandled imports returning 0, so an IRX reading a memory card file (Sony's NETCNF
reading mc0:/BWNETCNF/BWNETCNF) "opened" fd 0 and read nothing.

Now open (4), close (5), read (6), write (7), lseek (8), ioctl (9), remove (10), mkdir (11), rmdir (12), dopen (13),
dclose (14), dread (15), getstat (16), chstat (17) and format (18) (ps2sdk ioman.h) find the device by the name
before the unit number and ':', fill an iop_file_t {mode, unit, device, privdata} from a 32-slot table and call
the device's function from its iop_device_ops_t with the path after ':'. The call runs on the caller's own thread
(pc moves to the function, gp is the device's, ra a sentinel): a driver that waits for hardware, as MCMAN waits
for the card, blocks that thread while the others run. At the sentinel ioman restores the caller's ra and gp and
turns the result into the caller's: open/dopen return the fd (an error frees the slot), close/dclose and the
name-only operations free their slot, the others pass the result through. Unknown device -19, bad fd -9, table
full -24.

Test: iop_emulator_tests, a module registering device "tst" opens "tst3:/ab" with flags 1, reads, closes and opens
an unknown device: the device sees unit 3, flags 1 and path "/ab", fd 0, 4 bytes read, -19. Fails without: IOP
4/5.
